# The gate on an inlined function LOCAL's value at call entry.
#
# An `automatic` function local has NO value when the call starts.  The reader
# used the local's OWN WIRE as that entry value, and the wire is driven by the
# very process reading it -- so a local READ BEFORE IT IS WRITTEN closed a
# combinational cycle, and `check` reported one logic loop PER BIT: 32 here,
# and 32 in RSD FPExecutionStage, where read_slang reports 0 (it materialises
# the undefined entry value as a constant X, per the LRM).
#
# The DUT is otherwise clean, so `check -assert` is exactly this gate: it fails
# on the 32 loops without the fix and passes with it.
#
# A formal miter CANNOT gate this -- the module stays equivalent either way,
# and yosys itself labels each report "cell's internal connectivity
# overapproximated; loop may be a false positive".  That is precisely why the
# RSD sweep's formal column PROVED while the netlist carried 32 loops, and why
# this test asserts on netlist SHAPE instead.
read_uhdm slpp_all/surelog.uhdm
hierarchy -check -top func_local_read_before_write_loop
flatten; proc; opt -fast
check -assert
